{
  "case_id": "2005-05-18",
  "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "RAYMOND G. KUNTZ, ESQ., Bedford Village, New York; on behalf of the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Raymond G. Kuntz)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute awarding attorneys' fees as part of the costs to the prevailing parents provides a clear rule, imposes a certain obligation. It should not be expanded to include fees for expert witnesses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Raymond G. Kuntz)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Expert fees are not a part of attorneys' fees. Expert fees are not costs. The statute contains no reference to expert fees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first in Arlington Central School District Board of Education v. Murphy. Mr. Kuntz."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think the right includes any costs other than statutory costs, any expenses?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (David B. Salmons)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court should give the attorneys' fee provision of IDEA the same construction it gave the nearly identical language of section 1988 in Casey and hold that an award of attorneys' fees as part of the cost does not include expert fees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Salmons",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SALMONS: That -- that is correct.\nDuring the administrative proceeding and in the -- and\nin the district court, there was no attorney here.\nBut -- but I think there's one important\nthing to keep in mind about that is that that's --\nCongress expected that that would be the result."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: -- an argument, a perfectly\nfair argument, can be made, whether -- whether you find\nit dispositive or not, that everything that goes into a\ncommittee report of one house cannot simply be taken as\na literal reflection of the thinking -- the -- the\nactual thinking of -- of everybody on that committee,\nlet alone a whole house."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would you read the phrase from the conference report as a limitation? That is, that -- we're trying to figure out what the Congress meant by the phrase costs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, speaking of that -- of that language, that attorneys' fees may be awarded as part of costs, does that suggest -- it doesn't say directly that costs may be awarded. Does that suggest that the attorneys' fees are simply to be regarded as another element of costs that -- that may be awarded under the costs statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the authorization to pay costs, to pay those costs that include expert fees?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But where is the authorization to pay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. KUNTZ",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Shifting the costs to the school district of experts' fees will also shift scarce public resources away from the point where it's most effective, at the stage when the parent meets with the IEP team to resolve the differences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-05-18",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f9f97030f370fb133828d0b2d93a4a684f008801756df5434729a6a74ab33c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f9f97030f37-0002-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
